.TH tokenizer_peek 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/tokenizer"
.SH NAME
tokenizer_peek \- Peek at the next token from a tokenizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/tokenizer.h>
.sp
.BI "int tokenizer_peek(tokenizer* t)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function .BR tokenizer_peek () allows you to peek at the next token from a tokenizer without advancing the tokenizer. The function takes the following parameter:
.sp
1. A pointer to the tokenizer.
.sp
The function returns the next token as an int value.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The next token as an int value, or -1 if the end of the input is reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for this function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B tokenizer
